IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nz-nouns`
IMPORT `nz-part2-definitions`

-- Tests for nz-part2-definitions.l4 (ss 13 to 23, except the time rules in nz-interpretation-time.l4).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 13 -- New Zealand, the islands, and the territorial limits`

-- src:128 | New Zealand or similar words referring to New Zealand, when used as a territorial description,—
-- src:129 | means the islands and territories within the Realm of New Zealand; but
-- src:130 | does not include the self-governing State of the Cook Islands, the self-governing State of Niue, Tokelau, or the Ross Dependency
-- src:131 | North Island or Te Ika-a-Māui, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the North Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- "means the islands and territories within the Realm of New Zealand; but does not include the self-governing State of the Cook Islands,
-- the self-governing State of Niue, Tokelau, or the Ross Dependency".
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the island commonly known as the North Island` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `an island adjacent to the North Island` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the island commonly known as the South Island` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `an island adjacent to the South Island` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `another island or territory within the Realm of New Zealand` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the self-governing State of the Cook Islands` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the self-governing State of Niue` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `Tokelau` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `the Ross Dependency` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is within New Zealand as a territorial description` `a place outside the Realm of New Zealand` EQUALS FALSE

-- src:131 | North Island or Te Ika-a-Māui, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the North Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- src:151 | South Island or Te Waipounamu, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the South Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- North Island: the island commonly known as the North Island and the islands adjacent to it; likewise the South Island.
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `the island commonly known as the North Island` EQUALS `North Island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `an island adjacent to the North Island` EQUALS `North Island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `the island commonly known as the South Island` EQUALS `South Island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `an island adjacent to the South Island` EQUALS `South Island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `another island or territory within the Realm of New Zealand` EQUALS `Neither island`
#ASSERT `which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` `Tokelau` EQUALS `Neither island`

-- src:152 | territorial limits of New Zealand, limits of New Zealand, or a similar expression, when used as a territorial description, means the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand
#ASSERT `the territorial limits of New Zealand are` EQUALS "the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand"

§ `Section 13 -- person, repeal`

-- src:134 | person includes a corporation sole, a body corporate, and an unincorporated body
-- "person includes a corporation sole, a body corporate, and an unincorporated body": a natural person is not named, so the text is silent.
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a corporation sole` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `an unincorporated body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as a person under section 13` `a natural person` EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:145 | repeal, in relation to any legislation, includes—
-- src:146 | expiry (or any other lapsing or ceasing of effect); and
-- src:147 | revocation; and
-- src:148 | replacement
-- "repeal, in relation to any legislation, includes expiry (or any other lapsing or ceasing of effect); revocation; and replacement".
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `repeal in the ordinary sense` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `expiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `another lapsing or ceasing of effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `revocation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `replacement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as repeal under section 13` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 13 -- public notification, Proclamation, proceeding, writing`

-- src:141 | public notification, public notice, or a similar expression in relation to an act, a matter, or a thing, means a notice published—
-- src:142 | in the Gazette; or
-- src:143 | in 1 or more newspapers circulating in the area to which the act, matter, or thing relates or in which it arises; or
-- src:144 | on an Internet site that is administered by or on behalf of the person who must or may publish the notice, and that is publicly available as far as practicable and free of charge
-- A notice published (a) in the Gazette; or (b) in 1 or more newspapers circulating in the area; or (c) on an Internet site administered by or
-- on behalf of the person who must or may publish it, publicly available as far as practicable and free of charge.
-- Fields: Gazette; newspaper; Internet site administered by or for the publisher; publicly available; free of charge.
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- src:140 | Proclamation means a Proclamation made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand and (if it is not legislation) published in the Gazette
-- A Proclamation made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand and (if it is not legislation) published in the Gazette.
-- Arguments: made and signed under the Seal; it is legislation; published in the Gazette.
#ASSERT `is a Proclamation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Proclamation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Proclamation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a Proclamation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:137 | proceeding means a proceeding (whether civil, criminal, disciplinary, or other, at any stage, and interlocutory or main)—
-- src:138 | in or before a court or tribunal, or before a person acting judicially; or
-- src:139 | of a person or body performing administrative functions, investigative functions, or both
#ASSERT `is a proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a proceeding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a proceeding` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:159 | writing means representing or reproducing words, figures, or symbols in a visible and tangible form and medium (for example, in print) (but see Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017, which provides for meeting written requirements by electronic means).
-- Representing or reproducing words, figures or symbols in a visible and tangible form and medium.
-- Print and other things fixed on paper or an object are visible and tangible. Words only spoken are not visible. Words shown only on a screen are visible but the Act does not say a screen is tangible: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `is writing` TRUE `in print` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is writing` TRUE `written or typed on paper` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is writing` TRUE `fixed on a physical object` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is writing` FALSE `in print` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is writing` TRUE `spoken only, or otherwise not visible` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is writing` TRUE `shown only on a screen` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is writing` FALSE `shown only on a screen` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 13 -- member lookups for the definitions that list things`

-- Expected values decided from the words of each definition: "means" is closed (off the list is JUST FALSE), "includes" and "means ... and include" are open (off the list is NOTHING).
-- src:111 | Act means an Act—
-- src:112 | of the Parliament of New Zealand; or
-- src:113 | of the General Assembly
#ASSERT `counts as an Act under section 13` `an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand or of the General Assembly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an Act under section 13` `an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an Act under section 13` `an Act of the General Assembly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an Act under section 13` `a regulation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as an Act under section 13` `a Bill that has not been enacted` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as an Act under section 13` `an instrument of another kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:119 | enactment means the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation
#ASSERT `counts as an enactment under section 13` `the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an enactment under section 13` `the whole of an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an enactment under section 13` `a part of an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an enactment under section 13` `any secondary legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an enactment under section 13` `a Bill before it is enacted` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as an enactment under section 13` `an instrument that is not legislation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:120 | Gazette means the New Zealand Gazette (or a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette) published or purporting to be published under the authority of the New Zealand Government
#ASSERT `counts as the Gazette under section 13` `the New Zealand Gazette (or a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette)` `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Gazette under section 13` `the New Zealand Gazette` `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Gazette under section 13` `a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette` `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Gazette under section 13` `another gazette or journal` `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the Gazette under section 13` `the New Zealand Gazette` `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the Gazette under section 13` `a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette` `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:115 | Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth mean a country that is a member of the Commonwealth; and include a territory for the international relations of which the member is responsible
#ASSERT `counts as a Commonwealth country or part of the Commonwealth under section 13` `a country that is a member of the Commonwealth` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as a Commonwealth country or part of the Commonwealth under section 13` `a territory for the international relations of which a member of the Commonwealth is responsible` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as a Commonwealth country or part of the Commonwealth under section 13` `a place that is neither` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:132 | office includes position
#ASSERT `counts as an office under section 13` `an office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an office under section 13` `a position` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an office under section 13` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:121 | Governor-General in Council or a similar expression means the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council
#ASSERT `counts as the Governor-General in Council under section 13` `the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Governor-General in Council under section 13` `the Governor-General acting alone` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the Governor-General in Council under section 13` `the Executive Council acting alone` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the Governor-General in Council under section 13` `anyone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:135 | prescribed means prescribed by or under legislation
#ASSERT `counts as prescribed under section 13` `prescribed by or under legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as prescribed under section 13` `prescribed by legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as prescribed under section 13` `prescribed under legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as prescribed under section 13` `prescribed by regulations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as prescribed under section 13` `prescribed by a private contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as prescribed under section 13` `prescribed by anything else` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:118 | department, in relation to any legislation, means the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture (as named in Part 1, 2, or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020) that, with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation
-- src:126 | Ministry, in relation to any legislation, means the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture (as named in Part 1, 2, or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020) that, with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture named in Part 1, 2 or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `a departmental agency named in Part 2 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `an interdepartmental venture named in Part 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `a body that Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020 does not name` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` `a departmental agency named in Part 2 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:125 | Minister, in relation to any legislation, means the Minister of the Crown who, under the authority of a warrant or with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation
#ASSERT `counts as the Minister under section 13` `the Minister of the Crown who, under the authority of a warrant or with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Minister under section 13` `a Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the administration of the legislation under the authority of a warrant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Minister under section 13` `a Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the administration of the legislation with the authority of the Prime Minister` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as the Minister under section 13` `a Minister of the Crown who is not responsible for the administration of the legislation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as the Minister under section 13` `a person who is not a Minister of the Crown` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:115 | Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth mean a country that is a member of the Commonwealth; and include a territory for the international relations of which the member is responsible
-- src:121 | Governor-General in Council or a similar expression means the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council
-- src:128 | New Zealand or similar words referring to New Zealand, when used as a territorial description,—
-- src:131 | North Island or Te Ika-a-Māui, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the North Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- src:141 | public notification, public notice, or a similar expression in relation to an act, a matter, or a thing, means a notice published—
-- src:151 | South Island or Te Waipounamu, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the South Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- src:152 | territorial limits of New Zealand, limits of New Zealand, or a similar expression, when used as a territorial description, means the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `public notification` EQUALS JUST "public notification"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `public notice` EQUALS JUST "public notification"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `an expression similar to public notification` EQUALS JUST "public notification"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `Governor-General in Council` EQUALS JUST "Governor-General in Council"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `an expression similar to Governor-General in Council` EQUALS JUST "Governor-General in Council"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `New Zealand` EQUALS JUST "New Zealand"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `words similar to New Zealand` EQUALS JUST "New Zealand"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `territorial limits of New Zealand` EQUALS JUST "territorial limits of New Zealand"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `limits of New Zealand` EQUALS JUST "territorial limits of New Zealand"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `an expression similar to territorial limits of New Zealand` EQUALS JUST "territorial limits of New Zealand"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `North Island` EQUALS JUST "North Island"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `Te Ika-a-Māui` EQUALS JUST "North Island"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `South Island` EQUALS JUST "South Island"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `Te Waipounamu` EQUALS JUST "South Island"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `Commonwealth country` EQUALS JUST "Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `part of the Commonwealth` EQUALS JUST "Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth"
#ASSERT `the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` `an expression that no definition in section 13 names` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 14 -- Meaning of de facto relationship`

-- src:160 | 14 Meaning of de facto relationship
-- src:161 | In any legislation, de facto relationship means a relationship between 2 people (regardless of their sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity) who—
-- src:162 | live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union; and
-- src:163 | are not married to, or in a civil union with, each other; and
-- src:164 | are both aged 16 years or older.
-- src:165 | However, a relationship involving a person aged 16 or 17 years is not a de facto relationship unless that person has obtained consent for the relationship in accordance with section 46A of the Care of Children Act 2004.
-- src:166 | In determining whether 2 people live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union, the court or person required to determine the question must have regard to—
-- src:167 | the context, and the purpose of the law, in or for which the question is to be determined; and
-- src:168 | all the circumstances of the relationship.
-- src:169 | A de facto relationship ends if—
-- src:170 | the de facto partners cease living together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union; or
-- src:171 | one of the de facto partners dies.
-- Fields: age of first, age of second, live together as a couple, married or in a civil union with each other, consent obtained where either is 16 or 17.
-- Two adults living together, not married: a de facto relationship.
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 30, 30, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Both aged 18 (the first age at which no consent is needed): no consent needed.
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 18, 18, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- One aged 17 and no consent: not a de facto relationship; with consent: it is.
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 17, 18, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 17, 18, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Aged 16 (the minimum): with consent yes, without consent no.
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 16, 40, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 16, 40, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 16, 16, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Under 16: never, even with consent (the age limit is not displaced by (2)).
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 15, 40, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 40, 15, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Married or in a civil union with each other: not a de facto relationship.
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 30, 30, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Not living together as a couple.
#ASSERT `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF 30, 30, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- src:166 | In determining whether 2 people live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union, the court or person required to determine the question must have regard to—
-- src:167 | the context, and the purpose of the law, in or for which the question is to be determined; and
-- src:168 | all the circumstances of the relationship.
#ASSERT `what must be had regard to in deciding whether 2 people live together as a couple` EQUALS LIST "the context, and the purpose of the law, in or for which the question is to be determined", "all the circumstances of the relationship"

-- src:169 | A de facto relationship ends if—
-- src:170 | the de facto partners cease living together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union; or
-- src:171 | one of the de facto partners dies.
-- Ends if the partners cease living together as a couple, or one of them dies.
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship ends` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship ends` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship ends` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship ends` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:117 | de facto partner means a person who is a party to a de facto relationship (as defined in section 14)
#ASSERT `both people are de facto partners` (`Relationship between two people` OF 30, 30, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `both people are de facto partners` (`Relationship between two people` OF 30, 30, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 15 -- Meaning of step-parent, etc`

-- src:172 | 15 Meaning of step-parent, etc
-- src:173 | The relationship of step-parent, stepson, stepdaughter, or any other relationship described by a word containing the prefix step, may be established by civil union or by de facto relationship as well as by marriage.
#ASSERT `a step relationship may be established by` `marriage` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a step relationship may be established by` `civil union` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a step relationship may be established by` `de facto relationship` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a step relationship may be established by` `none of these` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 16 -- References to specific gender or kind of person include others`

-- src:174 | 16 References to specific gender or kind of person include others
-- src:175 | Words denoting a gender include every other gender.
-- src:176 | Words denoting a natural person by referring to a gender (for example, he or she) or words referring to persons generally (for example, someone or people) include a corporation sole, a body corporate, and an unincorporated body if capable of referring to a corporation sole, a body corporate, or an unincorporated body.
-- src:177 | Words denoting a corporation sole, a body corporate, or an unincorporated body include a natural person if capable of referring to a natural person.
-- (1) Words denoting a gender include every other gender.
#ASSERT `words denoting the gender` `the male gender` `include the gender` `the female gender` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting the gender` `the male gender` `include the gender` `any other gender` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting the gender` `the female gender` `include the gender` `the male gender` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting the gender` `any other gender` `include the gender` `the male gender` EQUALS TRUE

-- (2) Words denoting a natural person include a corporation sole, a body corporate and an unincorporated body, if capable of referring to them.
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a natural person by referring to a gender or to persons generally` `include` `a corporation sole` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a natural person by referring to a gender or to persons generally` `include` `a body corporate` `if capable of referring to it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a natural person by referring to a gender or to persons generally` `include` `an unincorporated body` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3) Words denoting a corporation sole, a body corporate or an unincorporated body include a natural person, if capable.
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a corporation sole, a body corporate or an unincorporated body` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a corporation sole, a body corporate or an unincorporated body` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a corporation sole` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a corporation sole` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a body corporate` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a body corporate` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `an unincorporated body` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words denoting` `an unincorporated body` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not stated: a gender-word includes a body corporate; a corporation-word includes a body corporate (it already does); a natural-person word includes a natural person.
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a gender` `include` `a body corporate` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a corporation sole, a body corporate or an unincorporated body` `include` `a body corporate` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a corporation sole` `include` `a body corporate` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a body corporate` `include` `a body corporate` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `words denoting` `an unincorporated body` `include` `a body corporate` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `words denoting` `a natural person by referring to a gender or to persons generally` `include` `a natural person` `if capable of referring to it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 18 -- Parts of speech have corresponding meaning`

-- src:184 | 18 Parts of speech have corresponding meaning
-- src:185 | Parts of speech and grammatical forms of a word that is defined in any legislation have corresponding meanings in the same legislation.
#ASSERT `a part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 19 -- Words in singular include plural and vice versa`

-- src:186 | 19 Words in singular include plural and vice versa
-- src:187 | Words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular.
#ASSERT `words in the` singular `number include the` plural `number` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `words in the` plural `number include the` singular `number` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 20 -- Words used in secondary legislation or other instruments have the same meaning as in the empowering legislation`

-- src:188 | 20 Words used in secondary legislation or other instruments have same meaning as in empowering legislation
-- src:189 | A word or an expression used in secondary legislation, or in any instrument, has the same meaning as it has, from time to time, in the legislation under which the secondary legislation or instrument is made.
-- "from time to time": the meaning in the empowering legislation at the time asked about, not when the instrument was made.
#ASSERT `the meaning of a word used in secondary legislation or an instrument` "the meaning at making" "the meaning today" EQUALS "the meaning today"

§ `Section 21 -- Anything done under secondary legislation or other instrument is also done under the Act`

-- src:190 | 21 Anything done under secondary legislation or other instrument is also done under Act
-- src:191 | A reference to anything being done under an Act includes anything done under secondary legislation, or another instrument, that is made under that Act.
-- src:192 | Example
-- src:193 | An Act empowers regulations to authorise a regulator to set fees. The Act requires all fees paid under the Act to be paid to the Crown. The regulations require the regulator to set fees by issuing a notice. The fees set in the regulator’s notice are paid under the Act and so must be paid to the Crown.
-- The example: fees set in the regulator's notice (an instrument made under the regulations, made under the Act) are paid under the Act.
#ASSERT `it is done under the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it is done under the Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `it is done under the Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 22 -- Legislation not binding on the Crown`

-- src:194 | 22 Legislation not binding on the Crown
-- src:195 | No Act or part of an Act binds the Crown unless the Act (or other legislation) expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or part.
-- src:196 | No secondary legislation, or part of secondary legislation, made under an Act or part of an Act binds the Crown unless—
-- src:197 | the Act (or another Act) expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or part of the Act; or
-- src:198 | the Act or the secondary legislation (or any other legislation) expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the secondary legislation or part of the secondary legislation.
-- (1) An Act or part binds the Crown only if legislation expressly says so.
#ASSERT `an Act or part of an Act binds the Crown` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act or part of an Act binds the Crown` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (2) Secondary legislation binds the Crown only if (a) the Act expressly binds the Crown in the Act or part it is made under, or (b) legislation expressly binds the Crown in the secondary legislation.
#ASSERT `secondary legislation or a part of it binds the Crown` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation or a part of it binds the Crown` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation or a part of it binds the Crown` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation or a part of it binds the Crown` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 23 -- Examples do not limit provision`

-- src:199 | 23 Examples do not limit provision
-- src:200 | An example provided in legislation of the operation of a provision of the legislation does not limit the provision.
-- src:201 | See section 10, which includes examples as part of the text of legislation from which its meaning must be ascertained.
#ASSERT `an example limits the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an example limits the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 13 -- writing, and the reference to Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017`

-- src:159 | writing means representing or reproducing words, figures, or symbols in a visible and tangible form and medium (for example, in print) (but see Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017, which provides for meeting written requirements by electronic means).
#ASSERT `a requirement to put something in writing is met` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a requirement to put something in writing is met` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a requirement to put something in writing is met` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a requirement to put something in writing is met` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a requirement to put something in writing is met` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
